ny and rule  over all the worlds of the universe so  in an attempt to fulfill this prophecy  and give birth to the perfect androgyny  emperor magellan and empress magella  with the help of the best robot surgeons  and the best human doctors conceive  janus janna a pair of conjoined twins  who rule the universe while living  inside of an egg which protects them  from any human diseases so in the  metabarents we see the birth of the  emperor s and how crazy that was  the emperor s is a really interesting  and strange character i just love the  fact that they are both male and female  and that they live in an egg it's super  weird i also love the characters tonto  and lothar who are the little robotic  characters that are actually narrating  the story and i have to mention that the  world building in this is absolutely  fantastic jodarowski has multiple  graphic novels that are set in this  universe including the techno priest and  like i mentioned the inkle there's also  a sequel to the ankle and a prequel and  there's also a sequel to the meta barons  called the meta baron which i have not  read yet but i hope to get to eventually  jodorowsky's connected universe is  actually amazing and really interesting  and the best part about this book in  particular is that the art is absolutely  fantastic juan gimenez the artist did an  absolutely fantastic job and he did have  a lot to live up to i mean jodorowsky's  book the inkle was done by mobius one of  the greatest of all time but the art in  the meta barons does not fail to impress  so i hope that i'm convincing you to  read this graphic novel because if you  enjoy science fiction and you don't mind  it being a little bit weird then i  definitely think you should give it a  try now i've said before that i'm glad  jodorowsky's dune didn't get made and i  stand by that because if he had actually  tried to make this movie and failed one  we probably would have never gotten a  david lynch dune dennyville news dune  would have probably never happened we  would have missed out on countless great  science fiction movies from the 20th  century that just wouldn't have gotten  made if jodorowsky's dune hadn't fallen  apart and the ideas weren't split  amongst its different creatives there's  a reason that they call it the most  influential film  never made let's be honest jodorowsky's  dune would have just been too weird for  a mainstream audience in the 1970s  but it's not too weird for a graphic  novel released in the 90s and it's  definitely not too weird for a graphic  novel these days a major reason to be  happy that that movie never got off the  ground is that we get these fantastic  comic books that fully teleport you to  an immersive  fantastical galactic universe full of  weird and interesting groups and  individuals with weird and interesting  stories now i don't intend to give away  too many spoilers about the plot in this  video because i really want you guys to  check out this graphic novel and i do  intend on covering more of jodorowsky's  comic book universe in the future  so definitely pick up the meta barons if  you want a fun story with cool  characters set in a really great science  fiction setting  thank you guys so much for watching if  you want more science fiction videos  check out my channel and make sure you  like and subscribe for more quinn's  ideas just a heads up for those of you  that may be interested my next graphic  novel the lie behind the star is  launching february 2023 you can sign up  now to get on the email mailing list to  get notified as soon as it launches more  information on my website link in the  description thank you guys so much  [Music]  you

